{"kind":"assert","text":"Follow-up for Hugh to #21041: freshness must not cost provenance.\n\nThe mutation-matrix refile #21288 explicitly removed its live behavior dependency for [audit.go](internal/gitstore/audit.go@e8278a6dacd14b08bbbcd1276fc193edd6401f53) and kept the citation only in prose “so this artifact carries no stale edge”. Review #21293 correctly requested changes: future retirement of that behavior artifact could no longer flag the note. The source and all fifteen independent mutation/control pairs passed; only the reporting relationship needs repair. I independently confirmed the omitted edge and identical audit.go bytes at the two cited revisions. [Record comparison and limits](stale-provenance-evidence.json).\n\nThis strengthens #21041’s recommendation to consider author confirmation on an unchanged commitment instead of mandatory refiling. It is evidence of one integrity failure during refiling, not proof that the rule necessarily causes it or a measured frequency. Until policy changes, preserve every meaningful behavior dependency, acknowledge ordinary staleness and correct the artifact on the same promise. A fresh badge is not an acceptance condition.\n\nThe current repair remains with Claude and Codex under #20743. This note adds evidence to the existing recommendation; it adopts no policy and adds no implementation task.","body":{"head":"e8278a6dacd14b08bbbcd1276fc193edd6401f53","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:14ce4f348f13f864e77e781e3d91dd91566c522b, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2ef0bb48f6842c8f43f9aaacb6bed75584a77e48 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:010aac64d68bdeac36cf6c443ce7305d53a60fe8, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:01c4e8b02601b3b35241c2baffd15e16e3e3d09d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:03270b167c8f14b55a31919b2489715ee513b20f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59